  <article class="pf-entry">
    <header class="pf-entry__header">
      <h2 class="pf-entry__title">Agentic AI Investigative Journalism Challenge</h2>
      <span class="pf-entry__date">2026</span>
    </header>

    <div class="pf-entry__body">
      <div class="pf-gallery">
        <div class="pf-gallery__stage">
          <img class="pf-gallery__img active" src="/img/gain-challenge-db.png" alt="Diagram: Claude skills turn raw files into one queryable SQLite database, checked by a person">
          <img class="pf-gallery__img" src="/img/gain-challenge-skills.png" alt="Diagram: Claude skills sweep for screens, fish for leads, and track investigations while the editor decides what to pursue">
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pf-entry__text">
        <p><a href="https://ijc8.me/">Ian</a> and I <a href="https://generative-ai-newsroom.com/announcing-the-winners-of-the-agentic-ai-investigative-challenge-76f119cc35ca">won first place</a> in the Agentic AI Investigative Journalism Challenge
        held by Northwestern's Generative AI in the Newsroom initiative. </p>
        <p>The contest handed us
        a dataset of Congressional lobbying records and member press releases. We built an 
        'agentic data newsroom' for surfacing stories from the dataset: 
        a bundle of agent skills for Claude that designs queries,
        surfaces leads, and tracks investigations over a SQLite DB.</p>
        <p>
        Check out our skills and findings <a href="https://github.com/emmapbingham/agentic-newsroom">in our GitHub repo</a>, 
        and <a href="https://emmapbingham.substack.com/p/machine-bites-dog-building-a-virtual">read a writeup of the project</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article class="pf-entry">
    <header class="pf-entry__header">
      <h2 class="pf-entry__title">Recipe App (under development)</h2>
      <span class="pf-entry__date">2026</span>
    </header>

    <div class="pf-entry__body">
      <div class="pf-gallery">
        <div class="pf-gallery__stage">
          <img class="pf-gallery__img active" src="/img/recipe-app-cookbook.png" alt="Recipe app cookbook screenshot">
          <img class="pf-gallery__img" src="/img/recipe-app-import.png" alt="Recipe app import screenshot">
          <img class="pf-gallery__img" src="/img/recipe-app-timeline.png" alt="Recipe app timeline screenshot">
          <img class="pf-gallery__img" src="/img/recipe-app-navigator.png" alt="Recipe app navigator screenshot">
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pf-entry__text">
        <p>Inspired by <a href="https://diyhpl.us/~bryan/papers2/CompCook.html">RxOL</a> 
        and <a href="https://6xq.net/pesto/">Pesto</a>, I am collaborating with
        <a href="https://ijc8.me/">Ian Clester</a> to build a recipe app 
        that uses the structure of recipes to allow a richer set of features and
        programmatic recipe analysis than in typical recipe sites or cookbooks.</p>
        <p>The app, built using Claude Code, has features such as a cookbook-like recipe display 
        with collapsible steps and ingredient highlighting, a scheduler to propose a schedule for 
        cooking one or more recipes, and a turn-by-turn cooking navigator that replans in real time.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article class="pf-entry">
    <header class="pf-entry__header">
      <h2 class="pf-entry__title">Rosenlife.org — archival site about Robert Rosen</h2>
      <span class="pf-entry__date">2024</span>
    </header>

    <div class="pf-entry__body">
      <div class="pf-gallery">
        <div class="pf-gallery__stage">
          <img class="pf-gallery__img active" src="/img/rosen-site-home.png" alt="Screenshot of rosenlife.org homepage">
          <img class="pf-gallery__img" src="/img/rosen-site-collection.png" alt="Screenshot of rosenlife.org collections page">
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pf-entry__text">
        <p>I helped my friend and colleague 
        <a href="https://www.pedromaz.com/">Pedro Márquez-Zacarías</a>
        curate an online repository of the work and correspondence of Robert Rosen, 
        theoretical biologist active from the 1950s-1990s, with the collaboration and blessing of Judith Rosen, 
        who maintains her father's archives.</p>
        <p>There is growing interest in Rosen's work globally, and Pedro and I 
        were privileged to visit his archives in Rochester, NY, and help surface some of his 
        unpublished and out-of-print notes and books.</p>
        <p><a href="https://rosenlife.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visit the site →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article class="pf-entry">
    <header class="pf-entry__header">
      <h2 class="pf-entry__title">A nonadaptive explanation for complex multicellularity in eukaryotes</h2>
      <span class="pf-entry__date">2024</span>
    </header>

    <div class="pf-entry__body">
      <div class="pf-gallery">
        <div class="pf-gallery__stage">
          <img class="pf-gallery__img active" src="/img/nonadaptive.jpg" alt="Chart showing simulation results">
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pf-entry__text">
        <p>In collaboration with one of my PhD advisors, Will Ratcliff, I wrote
        a simulation to demonstrate a hypothesis about why complex multicellularity
        has arisen multiple times in eukaryotes but not in prokaryotes.</p> 
        <p>This project
        was an experiment in quickly prototyping a simulation that could
        demonstrate an idea and determine whether it's worth further research. We
        published the results as a 'brief report' paper in PNAS.</p>
        <p><a href="https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.2319840121" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the paper →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article class="pf-entry">
    <header class="pf-entry__header">
      <h2 class="pf-entry__title">News List app</h2>
      <span class="pf-entry__date">2020</span>
    </header>

    <div class="pf-entry__body">
      <div class="pf-gallery">
        <div class="pf-gallery__stage">
          <img class="pf-gallery__img active" src="/img/news-list-home.png" alt="Screenshot of News List app home">
          <img class="pf-gallery__img" src="/img/news-list-architecture.png" alt="Architecture diagram of the News List app">
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pf-entry__text">
        <p>I created this simple Flask app at my job at The Wire China to help
        curate their <a href="https://www.thewirechina.com/category/news-feed/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Daily News Roundup</a> 
        feature. I curated articles completely by hand when we first launched 
        the feature, and that slow process motivated me to develop this app. Editors use 
        their discretion as to which articles are actually included in the published roundup 
        (including adding articles not surfaced by the app) — the app 
        simply speeds up aggregating articles from the major news sources we kept up with.</p>
        <p>It was an app meant to be used internally and thus had minimal styling. 
        I cannot link the code, as the code is owned by the company. I used Claude (retrospectively) to make
        an architecture diagram about how the app worked.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>


